- Unknown token: float() fails -> ValueError. Note: float parses "nan", "inf", "infinity" — those are parseable by float, so allowed per spec ("parseable by float"). Fine.
- Insufficient operands: len(stack) < 2 check. Good.
- Leftover operands: len(stack) != 1 at end. Good.
- Returns float: stack[0] is a float since numbers are converted via float() and operations on floats yield floats. Good.

